= Run report: the extension (amendment 5), 2026-10-20 to 2026-10-27

*Descriptive.* What ran and what it recorded. Interpretation is in the study's
`README.md` and `REPORT.pdf`.

- *Study:* `research/gaudry_quartic_d4_exponent_20261015`, `PROTOCOL.md` amendments 5, 5a, 5b
  (amendment 5 and its predictions X1–X10 were committed before any extension run, at
  `8f15139b2`). Specs `specs/SPEC-<job>.json` generated by `make_specs_ext.sh`; curves
  `curves.tsv`; queue `jobs_ext.txt` (first order) and `jobs_ext2.txt` (the order run, amendment
  5a); runner `run_queue5.sh`; log `sessions/queue.log`; launch notes `sessions/LAUNCH5.txt`.
- *Binary:* the same `ecbench` as the first 72 jobs (sha256 `8627cd29…0aa3`), not rebuilt.
- *Host:* Claude Code cloud container, rustc 1.97.0. The CPU set changed during the run (four
  CPUs at launch, then one, two, four again) and the container was restarted three times. Every
  session ran with `--allow-busy`: isolation earned L0 (46 records) or L1 (8) on the index-calculus
  records. `S` is a count (`priced_by = counted`) and does not depend on wall time, which is
  descriptive only.
- *Workloads:* `fp4_torsion(p, start seed, 16)`; chain-2 and chain-3 curves from `curves.tsv` for
  the plain arm and the rho-only runs, the original curves (start seed 1) for the rest; target seeds
  `2026102000000 + 100000·chain + 10p + t` (plain, new curves), `2026102990000 + 10000·chain + p`
  (rho-only, 16 targets), and the original `2026101500000 + 10p + t` for the paired and third-target
  jobs; measurement seed `202610150`.
- *Arms:* `rho-neg`; `ic-d4-w` (`linalg=wiedemann`), `ic-d4-lp2` and `ic-d4-lp1`
  (`large_primes=2`, `1`), the oracle `gaudry-d4:macaulay=26,weighted=1,chains=1,sparsest=1,replay=1,charge_unsolved=1`
  and base `fghr-y-line:zero=1` throughout.

== Runs requested and completed

74 sessions requested, *74 completed, all verified* (`[d]G = Q`): 20 rho-only sessions of 16
targets (320 verified rho runs); 54 sessions with an index-calculus arm and its paired rho record
(44 `ic-d4-w`: 40 on the new curves, 4 third targets; 6 `ic-d4-lp2`: `p = 401, 509, 701` ×2; 4
`ic-d4-lp1`: `p = 197, 293` ×2). No job was left unrun; `sessions/NOT_RUN5.txt` does not exist.
*Interruptions* (counts are unaffected): the first launch (2026-10-20T06:05Z) lost its jobs to a CPU
set that shrank to one CPU, so jobs assigned to missing CPUs ended in two seconds with no session
(amendment 5a); the container was restarted between 2026-10-21 and 26, at about 14:47Z on
2026-10-26 and at about 00:45Z on 2026-10-27, each time losing the jobs in flight (three third-target
jobs, then three large-prime jobs after 20 minutes, among them); they were rerun. The half-written
sessions and failed-launch logs are in `sessions-interrupted/`.

